{"author":"rebar-bridge[bot]","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1795404829056945002,"compiled_state":{"alias":"corrupting-plaster-seagull","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":2,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"5a0ee2157d086886990d2b50382eb06b2e8c43ca7f6e4b0ddd2701e3f7054461","event_uuid":"50aa8163-2df8-4588-b579-85ed5a32f2bb","position":{"commit_sha":"d1ec81d2b5b95b7ad09b09f30bc907aa0dd923d0","position":"1795404802912952001-50aa8163-2df8-4588-b579-85ed5a32f2bb"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIMQNvvCya66a6YyDlxwkxjjJPN3uaFI+QD3OjyC8e1UF rebar-mac-492a5c71 joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com 20261119"},{"content_hash":"cb762f997a0fd7dc5bec0133c7a1230fd681296369ac3c7e388bc887a5bd6da4","event_uuid":"0c93e470-7ead-4f75-8142-6e61ebfda168","position":{"commit_sha":"a2bcd576adc928959ffedc4b78e81d168514afb5","position":"1795404829056945001-0c93e470-7ead-4f75-8142-6e61ebfda168"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIMQNvvCya66a6YyDlxwkxjjJPN3uaFI+QD3OjyC8e1UF rebar-mac-492a5c71 joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com 20261119"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1795404802912952001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"0c93e470-7ead-4f75-8142-6e61ebfda168","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"7bef-6755-be56-4a43"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nFound while fixing hilarious-loony-crayfish (2026-11-22). `rebar init`'s own bootstrap git calls go through `init._git` (`run_git_write`, check=False), and callers read a watchdog timeout (exit 124, empty stdout) as an answer. Example: `_ensure_branch_user_config` treats a timed-out `config user.email` as unset and issues 4 more config calls; the `commit.gpgsign`/`tag.gpgsign` writes in `_mount_or_create_branch` discard their results. On a stalled filesystem each sequential call pays its own 120 s bound. Reproduced with a git shim that stalls tracker `git config`: the store fixture of tests/unit/test_attestation_signing.py hit its 300 s pytest-timeout inside `_ensure_branch_user_config`.\n\nSimply raising from `init._git` is not safe: it also serves the auto-init predicates (`pending_init_is_symlink`, `pending_init_attaches_to_existing`, `pending_init_remote_unreachable`) called from `_cli/_init.py` without a handler, and init's rebase recovery catches `Exception`. Stopping after `worktree add --orphan` but before the initial commit leaves a tracker that the next `rebar init` treats as already initialized, so the bootstrap steps never re-run.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A timed-out git in init's bootstrap is not treated as success or as an unset value.\n- [ ] A stalled filesystem costs `rebar init` at most one git bound before it reports the failure.\n- [ ] An init stopped mid-bootstrap is completed by the next `rebar init`.","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"75fe-db94-fcee-44da","ticket_type":"bug","title":"rebar init bootstrap reads a timed-out git as an answer and pays one 120 s bound per call","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["50aa8163-2df8-4588-b579-85ed5a32f2bb","0c93e470-7ead-4f75-8142-6e61ebfda168"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1795404829056945002,"uuid":"49112511-8f30-4f5b-b990-bd38557cd3c1"}